hey guys it's angelico with max tech and  i've been using the galaxy z flip 4 for  about a week now and i want to talk  about my experience with using a flip  phone for the first time both the  positives and the negatives and if i can  see myself buying one of these in the  future first i want to start with the  design and how different using this  thing is compared to my iphone  as far as quality it is amazing it's so  solid it feels great in the hand it's  gorgeous and unlike the iphone its frame  does not collect fingerprints at all  which makes it look really clean now the  main aspect of this phone is of course  that it can be folded and compact  carrying it in my pockets it's  definitely thick and not the most  comfortable phone to have in your jeans  however for guys that have more loose  pockets the flip is actually more  comfortable to carry in your front  pockets because it does not jam into  your body like bigger phones do along  with that in looser clothes like  sweatpants my iphone would fall out of  my pocket every time i get in and out of  my car but the flip did not it stayed in  every time which was really nice now i  wasn't expecting the hinge to be as  sturdy and high quality as it is  this thing stays in literally any  position you want without budging but  the downside with that is that it's  really hard to get open with one hand  which really bothered me day to day as  in order to use it you had to get it  open first which is a feat along with  that i don't have the biggest hands and  this phone is pretty big it's a lot  taller than my iphone which makes it  really hard to use with one hand for one  the volume buttons are almost all the  way at the top of the frame which is  extremely annoying i wish they were  lower where the 5g antenna or  fingerprint sensor is speaking of the  sensor i hate that it's built into the  power button and i wish i had an under  display scanner instead that would make  it a lot more convenient to use because  of that i've been using the facial  recognition option instead even though  it's not as secure as apple's face id  now onto the display i wasn't sure how  i'd feel about the crease but after  using it i actually love it it's  extremely subtle and doesn't bother me  in the slightest when scrolling through  text you can't see it at all it's  seamless however a little thing that  annoys me is the way that the screen  protector has this cut out for the front  camera  it's really distracting and it sticks  out like a sore thumb compared to the  quality of the rest of the phone in my  hands on comparison when i looked at the  brightness the flip was dramatically  dimmer than the iphone then i went and  saw that there is an extra brightness  toggle and after turning that on the  brightness reached about the same level  as the iphone this is something that  really bothers me about samsung why do i  have to go into the settings and turn on  all of these things just for the phone  to perform at the same level that an  iphone does out of the box the quality  of the display itself is amazing i have  zero complaints and it's so nice to  finally not have that horrid iphone  notch in the way the flip also has a 120  hertz display which is one of my  favorite features of all time  and with that it also has an always-on  display option that you can turn on  however that feature kind of goes to  waste because of the flip design and as  far as the speakers they are just as  good as the iphone 13 pro so  no compromises there  um  [Music]  now this phone has a usbc port which is  great for all the people that wish the  iphones had usb-c and are sick of  lighting being able to charge all your  devices without having to bring a bunch  of different cables everywhere is really  nice however for me personally it didn't  really make a difference because i  always use wireless charging and with  that i love how the cover display shows  your battery percentage while you're  charging so you can easily see when  you've charged it enough however one big  thing that i really missed having was  magsafe i always knew that magsafe was  one of my favorite unique features of  the iphone but not having it for a week  this phone really made me realize how  much i cannot live without it i use  magsafe every single day at work and  being able to see all of my  notifications and use my phone while  it's floating and charging right in  front of me is really nice it also means  that i always go home every day with a  full battery and at home if it ever gets  low i just throw it on my belkin three  in one that i love and i can still do  whatever i need while using it like  watching movies i also recently started  using this moft wallet and stand just to  pop up my phone and watching stuff and  it's so convenient that i don't think i  can ever go back and now let's talk  about the cameras and i'm honestly not  super impressed with them max vidimi and  i just did a blind camera comparison  with this flip the iphone 13 and the  pixel 6a  and the less expensive iphone 13 beat it  out by lot and the flip even lost by one  point to the super cheap budget pixel  phone not only that but it costs a  thousand dollars the same price as the  iphone 13 pro  which has an extra telephoto camera and  a lighter sensor which gives you really  good portrait photos so if the regular  iphone 13 beats it out then my 13 pro is  way ahead now one benefit with the flip  is that when it's closed you can use the  main camera on the back for selfies  resulting in much better quality images  honestly i don't really care too much  about it and i can't see myself using it  but if you can see yourself using it  then it'll definitely come in handy for  you so would i actually switch and use  this phone permanently  honestly no at first i was super excited  about the flip i thought it was the  coolest thing ever and then i would  absolutely love it but after actually  using it my mind has completely changed  about the biggest feature of this phone  that it folds using it day-to-day the  flip aspect of it hindered my experience  more than the benefits it provided it's  really hard to open with one hand and  while using it it's so long that i  literally cannot use it comfortably  without using both of my hands along  with that i don't carry around a purse  so i always keep my phone in my pocket  and this thing is just so thick that i  would rather just have an iphone that  sticks out and after being so excited  about the flip aspect  to me i've realized that it's kind of  more like a gimmick the z fold 4 makes a  lot more sense to me now because you get  this massive display that you cannot get  anywhere else but the flip left me  disappointed now that is not to say that  this is a bad phone at all and i'm not  trying to tell you that you will not  enjoy it  but i've just come to the conclusion  that it's not for me if you're out there  wanting to buy a flip phone or have used  one in the past and liked it then you  are definitely gonna love the z flip 4.  the quality is outstanding the display  speakers are incredible the crease is  super subtle and if you have big pockets  it's going to be super comfortable to  carry and just overall i think this  phone will have great longevity and  it'll look new and modern for years to  come so thank you for watching if you  guys like the channel click the button  above to subscribe and check out one of  those two videos over there this has  been angelica the editor with max tech  and i'll see you in the next video  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

